      },
      "text": "Section 1. All executive branch departments and agencies of the Federal \nGovernment shall be closed and their employees excused from duty for \nthe last half of the scheduled workday on Thursday, December 24, 2009, \nthe day before Christmas Day, except as provided in section 2 of this \norder."
    },
    {
      "char_end": 1529,
      "char_start": 1185,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:13523#sec2",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "Sec. 2.",
      "pdf_page": 1,
      "scope_id": "EO:13523#sec2",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "medium",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "74 FR 66563, PDF pages 1-1",
        "requires_page_check": true,
        "sha256": "747d55074f1861028e46c734d9a05529f59648ce3e09e70758f5e47307f2663d",
        "signing_date": "2009-12-11",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_13523.txt",
        "text_sha256": "7c9a322462cee0d8872b16b98281716343ead9fe183c1fedf2da208416f4933b",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2009-12-16/pdf/E9-30020.pdf"
      },
      "text": "Sec. 2. The heads of executive branch departments and agencies may deter-\nmine that certain offices and installations of their organizations, or parts \nthereof, must remain open and that certain employees must remain on \nduty for the full scheduled workday on December 24, 2009, for reasons \nof national security, defense, or other public need."
    },
    {
      "char_end": 1804,
